      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 499915185,
          "type": null,
          "body": "Looks like a good start to me, @AndersBroman can you also check this?\n\nBTW, the reason why it shows `UNKNOW` as opposed to `UNKNOWN` is due to the buffer being able to hold at most 7 chars + 1 terminating NUL byte.\n\nFrom ui/tap-sctp-analysis.h\n\n```c\ntypedef struct _sctp_assoc_info {\n...\n\tgchar\t   checksum_type[8];\n```\n\nFrom ui/tap-sctp-analysis.c\n\n```c\n        char str[] = \"UNKNOWN\";\n        g_strlcpy(data->checksum_type, str, strlen(str));\n```",
          "author": {
            "id": 2415432,
            "username": "Lekensteyn",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Peter Wu",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/efcf30db53f30b15e7c905ef37bd4dc44d87573bd92baf97cd707115d3fcd0c0?s=80&d=identicon",
